#. Tag: title
#: man-kate.1.docbook:8
#, no-c-format
msgid "KDE User's Manual"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: author
#: man-kate.1.docbook:9
#, no-c-format
msgid "&Lauri.Watts; &Lauri.Watts.mail;"
msgstr "&Lauri.Watts; &Lauri.Watts.mail;"

#. Tag: refentryinfo
#: man-kate.1.docbook:9
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<date>June 07, 2005</date> <productname>K Desktop Environment</productname>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: command
#: man-kate.1.docbook:15 man-kate.1.docbook:20
#, no-c-format
msgid "kate"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: manvolnum
#: man-kate.1.docbook:16
#, no-c-format
msgid "<manvolnum>1</manvolnum>"
msgstr "<manvolnum>1</manvolnum>"

#. Tag: refpurpose
#: man-kate.1.docbook:21
#, no-c-format
msgid "Advanced text editor for &kde;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: cmdsynopsis
#: man-kate.1.docbook:25
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<command>kate</command> <group choice=\"opt\"><option>-s, --start</option> "
"<replaceable> name</replaceable> </group> <group choice=\"opt\"><option>-u, "
"--use</option></group> <group choice=\"opt\"><option>-p, --pid</"
"option><replaceable> pid</replaceable></group> <group choice=\"opt"
"\"><option>-e, --encoding</option> <replaceable> name</replaceable></group> "
"<group choice=\"opt\"><option>-l, --line</option> <replaceable> line</"
"replaceable></group> <group choice=\"opt\"><option>-c, --column</option> "
"<replaceable> column</replaceable></group> <group choice=\"opt\"><option>-i, "
"--stdin</option></group> <arg choice=\"opt\">KDE Generic Options</arg> <arg "
"choice=\"opt\">Qt Generic Options</arg>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: man-kate.1.docbook:45
#, no-c-format
msgid "Description"
msgstr "Descripcion"

#. Tag: para
#: man-kate.1.docbook:46
#, no-c-format
msgid "&kate; is the &kde; Advanced Text Editor."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: man-kate.1.docbook:47
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kate; also provides the editor part for various applications, under the "
"name &kwrite;."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: man-kate.1.docbook:49
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Some of &kate;'s many features include configurable syntax highlighting for "
"languages ranging from C and C++ to <acronym>HTML</acronym> to bash scripts, "
"the ability to create and maintain projects, a multiple document interface "
"(<acronym>MDI</acronym>), and a self-contained terminal emulator."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: man-kate.1.docbook:56
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"But &kate; is more than a programmer's editor. Its ability to open several "
"files at once makes it ideal for editing &UNIX;'s many configuration files. "
"This document was written in &kate;."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: man-kate.1.docbook:66
#, no-c-format
msgid "Options"
msgstr "Opcions"

#. Tag: term
#: man-kate.1.docbook:70
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<option>-s</option>, <option>--start</option> <replaceable>name</replaceable>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: man-kate.1.docbook:72
#, no-c-format
msgid "Start &kate; with a given session."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: option
#: man-kate.1.docbook:75
#, no-c-format
msgid "-u, --use"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: man-kate.1.docbook:76
#, no-c-format
msgid "Use an already running &kate;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: man-kate.1.docbook:79
#, no-c-format
msgid "<option>-p, --pid</option> <replaceable> pid</replaceable>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: man-kate.1.docbook:81
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Only try to reuse kate instance with this <replaceable>pid</replaceable>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: man-kate.1.docbook:85
#, no-c-format
msgid "<option>-e, --encoding</option> <replaceable> name</replaceable>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: man-kate.1.docbook:87
#, no-c-format
msgid "Set encoding for the file to open"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: man-kate.1.docbook:87
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can use this to force a file opened in utf-8 format, for instance. (The "
"command <command>iconv -l</command> provides a list of encodings, which may "
"be helpful to you.)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: man-kate.1.docbook:93
#, no-c-format
msgid "<option>-l, --line</option> <replaceable> line</replaceable>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: man-kate.1.docbook:94
#, no-c-format
msgid "Navigate to this line"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: man-kate.1.docbook:97
#, no-c-format
msgid "<option>-c, --column</option> <replaceable> column</replaceable>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: man-kate.1.docbook:99
#, no-c-format
msgid "Navigate to this column"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: option
#: man-kate.1.docbook:102
#, no-c-format
msgid "-i, --stdin"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: man-kate.1.docbook:103
#, no-c-format
msgid "Read the contents of <filename>stdin</filename>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: man-kate.1.docbook:111
#, no-c-format
msgid "See Also"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: man-kate.1.docbook:113
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"More detailed user documentation is available from <ulink url=\"help:/kate"
"\">help:/kate</ulink> (either enter this <acronym>URL</acronym> into "
"&konqueror;, or run <userinput><command>khelpcenter</command> "
"<parameter>help:/kate</parameter></userinput>)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: man-kate.1.docbook:119
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"There is also further information available at <ulink url=\"http://kate.kde."
"org/\">the &kate; website</ulink>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: man-kate.1.docbook:124
#, no-c-format
msgid "Examples"
msgstr "Exemples"

#. Tag: para
#: man-kate.1.docbook:126
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To open a file named <filename>source.cpp</filename> at column 15, line 25, "
"in an existing &kate; window, you could use:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screen
#: man-kate.1.docbook:128
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<userinput><command>kate</command> <option>-c 15</option> <option>-l\n"
"25</option> <option>-u</option> <filename>source.cpp</filename></userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: man-kate.1.docbook:130
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you have an active internet connection, you can take advantage of &kde;'s "
"network transparency to open a file from an ftp site. If you do not have "
"write permission on the remote server, the file will be opened read only and "
"you will be prompted for a local filename to save to if you make changes. If "
"you do have write permission, changes will be saved transparently over the "
"network."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screen
#: man-kate.1.docbook:136
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<userinput><command>kate</command> <option><replaceable>ftp://ftp.kde.org/"
"pub/kde/README_FIRST</replaceable></option></userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: man-kate.1.docbook:154
#, no-c-format
msgid "Authors"
msgstr "Autors"

#. Tag: para
#: man-kate.1.docbook:155
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The maintainer of &kate; is &Christoph.Cullmann; &Christoph.Cullmann.mail;. "
"A comprehensive list of authors and contributors is available in the "
"complete user manual mentioned above."
msgstr ""
